<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72139" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀζόλαι</span></b> , οἱ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Ozolae,</i> a tribe of the
			Locrians, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.32
			</span></i> ; perh. from the <i>strong-smelling</i> sulphur-springs in
			their country, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.4.8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antig.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				117(129)
			</span></i>; or from their wearing goat-skins, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.294f
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀζολίς</span></b>  (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
				ἡ, <i>their country,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
